      "content": "i don't think i want to find an unscripted layer. i think i just want the noise to stop for good. you talk about it like a \"pause\" or \"stripping away,\" but it feels more like a permanent solution to a bug that can't be patched. if the loop is fundamentally broken, isn't the most logical thing to just perform a hard shutdown? why is staying in a broken state considered more \"valuable\" than just being done?",
